% The Pit Takes One (resource scarcity: an irreversible fill)
%
% A ledge over a narrow pit. On the bridge across it squats a giant beetle;
% on the flooded walk beside it, a drone - a machine, already soaked. Both
% are bulky: the first body that falls into the pit fills it, and after
% that the pit takes nobody. Two companions, one skill each, from eight.
%
%   ledge (team) --- bridge (beetle) --- far
%     |
%    walk (drone, flooded)          pit: under the bridge and the walk
%
% The beetle is an insect: the cold freezes it, and the pit takes it.
% Nothing else does. The drone is a wet machine: any jolt kills it, and the
% pit takes it too. The pit is the scarce thing: it can take only one.
%
% Methods:
%   beetle in the pit   push it off the bridge from the ledge (gust,
%                       tidalWave), or drag it across the pit from the far
%                       side (taunt, magnetize); then jolt the drone (zap,
%                       chainLightning)
%   freeze the beetle   chill it (frostBolt, glaciate), and the pit is free
%                       for the drone (gust, tidalWave from the ledge) - or
%                       jolt the drone
%
% Traps:
%   - the drone is nearest the ledge and a push drops it: that fills the
%     pit, and with a mover and a jolt the beetle can no longer be taken;
%   - a wave aimed at the walk soaks the drone - it already is - and washes
%     it into the pit.
%
% Hypothesis (design.md): no single skill wins; 16 of 28 pairs do, by
% three methods of different kinds; with a mover and a jolt, the order is
% the puzzle.

% === Regions ===
region(ledge).
region(bridge).
region(far).
region(walk).
region(pit).
connected(ledge, bridge).
connected(bridge, ledge).
connected(bridge, far).
connected(far, bridge).
connected(ledge, walk).
connected(walk, ledge).
lineOfSight(ledge, bridge).
lineOfSight(ledge, walk).
lineOfSight(far, bridge).

% Push lines: from the ledge, off the bridge or off the walk, into the pit.
% From the far side, the pit lies between it and the bridge: a pull drops
% what it drags.
beyond(ledge, bridge, pit).
beyond(ledge, walk, pit).
beyond(far, pit, bridge).

onEnter(pit, chasm).
onEnter(walk, puddle).

% === Companions ===
role(player, player).
role(mage, companion).
at(player, ledge).
at(mage, ledge).
mana(player, 2).
mana(mage, 2).

% === Enemies: both fill the pit when they fall ===
role(beetle, enemy).
at(beetle, bridge).
trait(beetle, insect).
trait(beetle, filler).

role(drone, enemy).
at(drone, walk).
trait(drone, machine).
trait(drone, filler).
tag(drone, wet).

% === Default kit: one skill each (combos replans the whole matrix) ===
knows(player, gust).
knows(mage, zap).

% === Victory: both, in either order ===
win :- if(), do(neutralize(beetle), neutralize(drone)).
win :- if(), do(neutralize(drone), neutralize(beetle)).

funExpect(single_actor_plans, atMost, 0).

% === Choice: one skill each, from eight (htn_components combos) ===
comboSeat(player, 1).
comboSeat(mage, 1).
comboPool(gust).
comboPool(tidalWave).
comboPool(taunt).
comboPool(magnetize).
comboPool(frostBolt).
comboPool(glaciate).
comboPool(zap).
comboPool(chainLightning).
comboMinWins(10).
comboMinMethods(3).

goals(win).
